                "headline": "Wind Advisory issued November 10 at 9:50PM AKST until November 11 at 12:00PM AKST by NWS Juneau AK",
                "description": "* WHAT...Southeast winds 15 to 25 mph with frequent gusts to 45 mph.\nSporadic gusts up to 55 mph.\n\n* WHERE...Annette Island, Ketchikan Gateway Borough, and Prince of\nWales Island.\n\n* WHEN...Until noon AKST Wednesday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Gusty winds will blow around unsecured objects. Tree\nlimbs could be blown down and a few power outages may result.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...A series of fronts will move across the area\nfrom Tuesday night through Wednesday. Winds slowly subside through\nlate Tuesday afternoon for a brief lull before another front moves\nover the area Tuesday night. This front will bring another round of\nstrong winds by early Wednesday morning into the afternoon across\nthe southern panhandle. Stay tuned to weather.gov/ajk for updates.\nStay tuned to weather.gov/ajk for updates.",
